  "_how_it_is_used": [
    "Canonical vein table of the pack. Read by startup_scripts/grindless/lib/tables.js (global.grindless.tables.veins), which feeds the vein sample items, and by server_scripts/grindless/data/veins.js, which derives the recipe data. Electric drills of later tiers must read the same table.",
    "id = GTM vein id without the '_vein' suffix ('magnetite_vein_ow' -> 'magnetite_ow'). The sample item is grindless:vein_sample_<id>.",
    "gtm = GTM vein id (gtceu:<gtm> in GTRegistries.ORE_VEINS). layer = stone | deepslate. minY/maxY = heightRangeUniform. spawnWeight = GTM vein weight.",
    "materials[].id = GTM material name. weight = layer weight (layered), block weight (dike, veined) or, for the classic generator (no weights in GTM), derived from its geometry.",
    "veined veins: materials with rare=true show up with probability rareChance, the others share the rest by weight (GTM rareBlockChance).",
    "colorMaterial = surface indicator rock of the vein in GTM; color = that material's GTM .color() (tint of the sample core).",
    "steelOnly is NOT stored: it is derived as maxY < 0 (deep veins need the steel drill bit)."
  ],
